Arjun was a 4-year Java dev. Like every dev, he hated one bug.
For 3 weeks this one error kept crashing the production app at exactly 2:17 AM:
NullPointerException at line 404 in UserService.javaNo one touched that code in months. Logs showed the user_id was always null.  
PMs were angry. Arjun was on night duty.On the 4th night, he decided to stay late and watch it happen live.
2:16... 2:17... crash.
He opened the debugger and stepped through. The user_id was being set by a cron job called AutoCleaner.Weird. He checked who wrote AutoCleaner.  
Author: a.arjunHe didn’t remember writing it. He searched git history.
Commit message: "Fix memory leak -Arjun"
Date: 2 years from now.His blood ran cold. He scrolled up. There were 20 more commits... all by him. All dated in the future.Then his phone buzzed. Unknown number.
Message: "Stop debugging. If you fix line 404, you erase me.  You, from 2028"Arjun stared at the screen. The bug wasn’t in the code.
The bug was that he was supposed to leave it there.He closed his laptop at 2:18 AM.
Some bugs exist so that future-you has a job.
